# Dev Dashboard — Project Rules

## Project Overview
React 18 dashboard for engineering team metrics. Vite + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS.

## Tech Stack
- React 18 with functional components and hooks
- TypeScript (strict mode) — no `any` types, ever
- Tailwind CSS for all styling — no inline styles, no CSS modules
- Recharts for data visualization
- Lucide React for icons

## Architecture
- `src/components/` — one component per file, named export, PascalCase filename
- `src/types/` — shared TypeScript interfaces, suffix with descriptive name (e.g., `dashboard.ts`)
- `src/data/` — mock data and constants, typed with interfaces from `types/`
- All components receive data via props — no direct data imports inside components

## Component Patterns
- Always use named exports: `export function ComponentName()`
- Define a `ComponentNameProps` interface for every component's props
- Use Tailwind utility classes exclusively — prefer `gap-*` over margins between siblings
- Rounded corners: `rounded-xl` for cards, `rounded-lg` for inner elements, `rounded-full` for avatars
- Shadows: `shadow-sm` default, `hover:shadow-md` for interactive cards
- Color palette: blue-500/600 primary, emerald-500 success, red-500 error, gray-50/100/400/500/900 for neutrals
- Use `transition-*` classes for hover/state changes
- Keep components under 80 lines — extract sub-components if longer

## Data & Types
- Every data structure must have a TypeScript interface in `src/types/`
- Mock data goes in `src/data/mockData.ts`, exported as named constants
- Use descriptive property names, not abbreviations

## When Adding New Features
- Create new types first in `src/types/`
- Add mock data in `src/data/mockData.ts`
- Create component(s) in `src/components/`
- Wire into `App.tsx` — follow existing grid layout patterns
- New metric cards should reuse the `MetricCard` component
